---
/**
 * What this site collects, which is nothing.
 *
 * **Rewritten by TK-31 for one false claim and one unsupportable one.** The
 * previous version ended with "Every page here was individually reviewed and
 * approved for publication. Material that was not approved is not represented
 * on this site in any form." The first sentence describes one owner's exporter
 * and is false of a build from a directory of Markdown; the second is *true*
 * and had been resting on the first, so it read as a consequence of a review
 * process rather than of what the build actually does.
 *
 * That distinction matters more here than on `/about/`. A privacy page is the
 * document a reader consults to decide whether to trust the rest, so a claim in
 * it that the tool cannot keep is worse than no page: it converts a technical
 * guarantee into a promise about someone's diligence, and a reader has no way
 * to tell which they were given.
 *
 * **Every claim below is a property this build enforces**, and each is scoped to
 * what is actually held. `tests/built-output.test.ts` asserts every `<script>`
 * in `dist/` is same-origin and none is inline; `public/_headers` sets a CSP
 * whose `script-src`, `style-src`, `font-src`, and `connect-src` are all
 * `'self'`. The absence of cookies and of analytics follows from there being no
 * server and no such script.
 *
 * **`img-src` is the one directive that is not `'self'`** — it permits `https:`,
 * so a note whose author embedded a remote image renders it, and that request
 * reaches a third party. Measured, not inferred. The page therefore says
 * "script, stylesheet, and font" where it once said "every asset", and names the
 * image case separately: the earlier wording was a claim this build does not
 * keep, on the page a reader consults to calibrate trust.
 *
 * The other thing this page cannot speak for is the host that serves the files,
 * so it says who that is and stops rather than promising on their behalf.
 *
 * See `about.astro` for why this is still a shipped page rather than a note
 * `init` seeds into the user's own repository.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { TITLE_SUFFIX } from '../lib/site.ts';
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy${TITLE_SUFFIX}`}
  description="No analytics, no comments, no third-party tracking."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>

    <p>
      There are no analytics on this site. No page view, click, scroll, reading time, or search
      query is measured, recorded, or reported anywhere.
    </p>

    <p>
      There are no comments, reactions, accounts, or sign-in. There is nothing to submit and no
      form to fill in.
    </p>

    <p>
      No third-party tracking runs here. There are no advertising or analytics scripts, no
      tracking pixels, no social widgets, and no embedded players. Every script, stylesheet, and
      font a page loads comes from this site's own address.
    </p>

    <p>
      Images are the exception, and only where a note's author linked one. A note that embeds an
      image hosted elsewhere renders that image from wherever it lives, so displaying it tells that
      host you loaded the page — the same as following a link there. Nothing on this site does that
      on its own; it happens only where the writing itself points outward.
    </p>

    <p>
      This site sets no cookies. Your theme and reader-mode choices are stored by your own browser,
      on your own device, and are never sent anywhere. Clearing your browser's site data removes
      them.
    </p>

    <h2>Search</h2>

    <p>
      Search runs entirely inside your browser against a search index served as a static file.
      Nothing you type is transmitted to this site or to anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2>What is unavoidable</h2>

    <p>
      Requesting a page from any website necessarily reveals your IP address and browser details to
      whoever serves it. This site is served by a static hosting provider, which may keep
      operational request logs of its own under its own policy. Nothing beyond that is collected by
      this site, which has no server of its own to collect it with.
    </p>

    <h2>Content</h2>

    <p>
      This site is generated from a set of notes, and a note excluded from it produces no page, no
      search entry, and no link. None of its content appears here. What can still appear is the
      words a published note used to refer to it: a link pointing at an excluded note keeps its own
      link text, which the author wrote. See <a href="/about/">About</a> for how that works.
    </p>

    <p>
      If any of this changes, this page changes with it.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
